title: Dealing with the Coalition
new-page: true
is-card: true
tags: govt_affairs
on-arrival: month_actions += 1; coalition_affairs_timer = 5
view-if: spm_in_government = 1 and coalition_dissent >= 1 and coalition_affairs_timer = 0
card-image: img/muller_cabinet.jpg

= Dealing with the Coalition

Our coalition is fracturing. The initial euphoric high of locking out the {!<span style="color: #22275C;"><strong>PEC</strong></span>!} has yielded to political stagnation, and the majority is locked in legislative paralysis. Unsurprisingly, {!<span style="color: #023CA7;"><strong>Earthist</strong></span>!} opportunists are exploiting these internal rifts to regain control. We must act quickly to restore unity among our partners.

How do we reduce tensions with the coalition?

- @mnlp_apeal_to_worse: {!<span style="color: #D3C24D;"><strong>MNLP</strong></span>!}: Appeal to the lesser evil.
- @mnlp_budget_cuts: {!<span style="color: #D3C24D;"><strong>MNLP</strong></span>!}: Cut the budget, where possible.
- @bring_down: Instead, we will bring down the government with a no-confidence vote, and call for new elections.
- @no_change: Take none of these actions.
- @easy_discard

@mnlp_apeal_to_worse
view-if: mnlp_in_government = 1
on-arrival: mnlp_relation -= 10; coalition_dissent -= 1
unavailable-subtitle: Our relationship with the {!<span style="color: #D3C24D;"><strong>MNLP</strong></span>!} is not high enough.
choose-if: mnlp_relation >= 30

The {!<span style="color: #D3C24D;"><strong>MNLP</strong></span>!} must face reality: either our moderate coalition holds the center, or the planet devolves into an armed militia war between the {!<span style="color: #22275C;"><strong>PEC</strong></span>!} and the radical {!<span style="color: #540808;"><strong>PLFM</strong></span>!}. Passing pro-worker legislation is the only rational strategy to keep the working masses invested in parliamentary democracy.

@mnlp_budget_cuts
view-if: mnlp_in_government = 1
on-arrival: capitalist_class_mnlp += 3; indipendent_capitalist_class_mnlp += 3; mnlp_relation += 5; coalition_dissent -= 2; technicians_spm -= 5; miners_spm -= 6; technicians_plfm += 5 if plfm_in_government == 0; miners_plfm += 6 if plfm_in_government == 0; plfm_relation -= 10 if plfm_in_government == 1; technicians_ffm -= 5 if plfm_in_government == 1; miners_ffm -= 6 if plfm_in_government == 1; coalition_dissent += 1 if plfm_in_government == 1; left_dissent += 10; progressist_dissent += 5; budget += 1
unavailable-subtitle: The {!<span style="color: #540808;"><strong>PLFM</strong></span>!} has promised to bring down the coalition, should this happen.
choose-if: plfm_relation >= 30 or plfm_in_government = 0 

The {!<span style="color: #D3C24D;"><strong>MNLP</strong></span>!} demands sweeping cuts to what they dismiss as "useless welfare programs, dangerous state subsidies, and reckless social spending." To stabilize the coalition and secure their cooperation, we have conceded to their austerity demands. Perhaps these funds can be redirected toward more important state initiatives down the line? [? if plfm_in_government == 1: Unsurprisingly, the {!<span style="color: #540808;"><strong>PLFM</strong></span>!} is fiercely fighting this decision, though when pressed on the floor, their leadership struggles to articulate precisely which "vital programs" are on the chopping block. ?]

@resources
subtitle: -2 resources
view-if: historical_mode = 0
unavailable-subtitle: Not enough resources (need 2).
choose-if: resources >= 2
on-arrival: resources -= 2; coalition_dissent -= 1

By transferring campaign funds to our coalition partners, we can make our policies more acceptable to them. Some would call this corruption, but perhaps it is necessary to save democracy.

@no_change

No. We will not do this.

@bring_down
subtitle: Bring down this government before our opponents do.
on-arrival: spd_in_government = 0; in_grand_coalition = 0; in_weimar_coalition = 0; chancellor = "Brüning"; chancellor_party = "Z"; next_election_time = time + 3 if next_election_time > time+3; next_election_month = month + 3 if next_election_time >= time+3; next_election_year = year if next_election_time >= time+3; next_election_year += 1 if next_election_month > 12; next_election_month -= 12 if next_election_month > 12; spd_toleration = 0; left_strength += 8; pro_republic -= 5; new_middle_spd -= 3; rural_spd -= 3; old_middle_spd -= 3; catholics_spd -= 3; reformist_dissent += 5

We have called for a vote of no confidence in ourselves, and have brought down this government. Chancellor [+ chancellor +] currently rules as acting chancellor.

New elections have been set for [+ next_election_month : month +] [+ next_election_year +].

